      "content": "that's a pretty interesting take. but doesn't characterizing it as a \"ruthless calculation of what the time demanded\" kind of brush off the actual human cost? like, if you bypass democracy and use war to force alignment, aren't you basically saying that stability is more important than people's right to self-determination? i don't see how that's anything other than a failure of leadership/morality.\n Singaporean scholars and modern political theorists would probably call that an authoritarian",
